{
  "tema": 5187,
  "slug": "subjuntivo-presente-haber",
  "titulo": "Conjugate haber in the present subjunctive",
  "subtitulo": "Ojalá haya olas: haya is the subjunctive of hay.",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "Haber has the stem hay- in the present subjunctive: haya, hayas, haya, hayamos, hayan. Alone, only haya is used (the subjunctive of hay).",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Haber** has an irregular stem, **hay-**, in the present subjunctive, with regular endings."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "haber"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "haya"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "hayas"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "haya"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "hayamos"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes, ellos",
              "hayan"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "On its own, only **haya** is used: it's the subjunctive of **hay** (_there is, there are_), and it stays singular: **ojalá haya olas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "All the forms are used with a past participle to build the **present perfect subjunctive**: **espero que hayas comido**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **hay** becomes **haya** the moment a wish or a doubt comes along."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Ojalá ==haya== buenas olas mañana.",
              "en": "I hope there are good waves tomorrow."
            },
            {
              "es": "No creo que ==haya== una boda tan bonita como la suya.",
              "en": "I don't think there's a wedding as beautiful as yours."
            },
            {
              "es": "Es esencial que ==haya== un acuerdo.",
              "en": "It's essential that there be an agreement."
            },
            {
              "es": "Quiero que ==haya== un buen presidente.",
              "en": "I want there to be a good president."
            },
            {
              "es": "No creo que ==haya== un buen sistema aquí.",
              "en": "I don't think there's a good system here."
            },
            {
              "es": "Espero que no ==haya== problemas con tu presentación.",
              "en": "I hope there aren't any problems with your presentation."
            },
            {
              "es": "Espero que el niño ==haya comido== bien.",
              "en": "I hope the boy has eaten well."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
